\caption{The base-four carry is $c(x,y)=\lfloor(x+y)/4\rfloor$. The rust cells mark pairs that produce one carry. For the triple $(3,2,1)$, the two parenthesisations give carry totals $1+0$ and $0+1$, both equal to $\lfloor6/4\rfloor$. This equality is the two-cocycle identity.}
